if (cfs_rq->avg.load_sum)
    return false;

if (child_cfs_rq_on_list(cfs_rq))
    return false;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the `cfs_rq` can be incorrectly marked as decayed if its child `cfs_rq` is unthrottled but not added to the list due to its `nr_running` being zero. This results in the parent `cfs_rq` not being properly represented in the scheduling hierarchy, leading to warnings about the scheduling list structure.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (child_cfs_rq_on_list(cfs_rq))
    return false;

static inline bool child_cfs_rq_on_list(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq) { ... }
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check to ensure that if a child `cfs_rq` is on the list, the parent `cfs_rq` will not be marked as decayed. This ensures that the parent is correctly represented in the scheduling hierarchy whenever one of its children is present, thus preventing the warnings related to the scheduling list structure.

